# Courier Dashboard – Account Profile Page Rule

## Objective

Build a complete, accessible, and visually polished Account Profile page for couriers within the Courier Dashboard at `/courier/profile`.
**No backend logic or API integration—focus is on layout, navigation, and user experience.**

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **State Management:** Zustand (if needed, for client-side state)
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions as per `premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc`
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast)

---

## 2. Route & Naming

- **Route:** `/courier/profile`
- **ID Prefix:** `parcego-courier-profile-[purpose]-[unique]`
- **Class Prefix (BEM):** `parcego-courier-profile__element--modifier`
- **Examples:**
  - `id="parcego-courier-profile-back-btn"`
  - `id="parcego-courier-profile-avatar-input"`
  - `class="parcego-courier-profile__card parcego-courier-profile__card--elevated"`

---

## 3. Page Structure & Features (UI Only)

### 3.1 Header Bar
- Back button to dashboard with icon and label; keyboard accessible
- Title: "Account Profile"
- Subtle page description
- Avatar thumbnail and availability badge

### 3.2 Profile Overview Card
- Avatar with mock upload (drag-and-drop or click to select)
- Name, Courier ID, status pill
- Quick actions: Edit Profile, Change Password, View Performance

### 3.3 Tabs
- Tabs: Profile, Security, Notifications, Availability, Vehicle
- Persist selected tab in client-state (Zustand optional)

### 3.4 Profile Tab (Form)
- Fields: Full Name, Email, Phone, Address
- Inline hints and validation messages (UI only)
- Primary Save button (shows mock toast/success banner)

### 3.5 Security Tab
- Change password button opens Dialog with fields: Current, New, Confirm
- Password requirements checklist (UI-only)
- Show/Hide password toggles

### 3.6 Notifications Tab
- Switches: Push, Email, In-app banners
- Frequency radio group: Immediate, Hourly, Daily Digest
- Sound/Vibration toggles (mobile-friendly)

### 3.7 Availability Tab
- Master availability Switch (Available/Unavailable)
- Optional schedule picker (Day rows with time ranges – UI only)
- Status preview banner with aria-live

### 3.8 Vehicle Tab
- Fields: Vehicle Type (Select), Plate Number, Color, Notes
- Upload area for vehicle photo (mock)

### 3.9 Stats Preview
- Mini cards: Deliveries, Rating, Hours Online
- Link to Performance Analytics `/courier/performance`

### 3.10 Logout
- Destructive button opens confirmation AlertDialog

---

## 4. Components to Use (shadcn/ui)

- `Avatar`, `Button`, `Badge`, `Card`, `Tabs`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `Label`, `Switch`, `Select`, `RadioGroup`, `Separator`, `Dialog`, `AlertDialog`, `DropdownMenu`, `Toast` (or `useToast`), `Skeleton`
- Use `Dialog` for Change Password; `AlertDialog` for Logout confirm
- Use `Skeleton` for mock-loading states of avatar and stats cards

---

## 5. Accessibility

- All form fields must pair `Label` and inputs with `htmlFor`/`id`
- Provide `aria-describedby` for helper text and error text
- Buttons and interactive icons must have `aria-label`
- Avatar upload dropzone must support keyboard: `tabIndex=0`, `onKeyDown` Enter/Space triggers file picker
- Use `aria-live="polite"` for non-blocking status updates (e.g., availability switch feedback)
- Meet WCAG AA contrast; ensure visible focus rings on all focusable elements
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: disable non-essential animations

---

## 6. Premium Transitions & Micro-interactions

- Use transition classes on interactive elements: `transition-all duration-200 ease-[var(--easing-smooth)]`
- Hover: soft elevation and subtle border/scale; Active: `scale-95`
- Entrance: fade+slide for cards and dialogs (opacity/translate only; no layout shift)
- Focus: ring and outline visible on keyboard navigation
- Avoid default translateY(-2px) on hover; use subtle shadow and border color shift instead

---

## 7. Validation UX (UI Only)

- Real-time validation styles on blur/change; show compact helper text under fields
- Error text pattern: concise, specific, accessible via `aria-live="polite"`
- Disable primary submit button only if form is clearly incomplete; otherwise allow click and show inline errors
- Success feedback: use Toast and/or inline success banner in the card header

---

## 8. Mock Data & State

- Provide constants for sample profile: name, phone, email, courierId, avatar URL, availability
- Provide constants for vehicle info and notification defaults
- Use local component state or Zustand for tab selection and switches
- No network calls; no persistence

---

## 9. Layout Blueprint

- Container: responsive max-w-6xl with padding
- Grid: `grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12`
  - Left column (lg:col-span-4): Overview card, Stats cards
  - Right column (lg:col-span-8): Tabs with forms
- Mobile: stack cards; Tabs become scrollable horizontally

---

## 10. Navigation

- Back button id: `parcego-courier-profile-back-btn` routes to `/courier`
- "View Performance" button routes to `/courier/performance`
- All navigations are client-side; use Next.js `useRouter`

---

## 11. ID, Class & Example Targets

- IDs
  - `parcego-courier-profile-header`
  - `parcego-courier-profile-avatar`
  - `parcego-courier-profile-availability-switch`
  - `parcego-courier-profile-tabs`
  - `parcego-courier-profile-form-save-btn`
  - `parcego-courier-profile-logout-btn`
- Classes
  - `parcego-courier-profile__card`
  - `parcego-courier-profile__stats-card`
  - `parcego-courier-profile__form-field`

---

## 12. Error, Empty & Loading States

- Show `Skeleton` while mock data loads (simulated with `useEffect` timeout)
- Empty avatar falls back to initials via `AvatarFallback`
- Failed image load shows fallback; show inline banner in overview card for any critical UI errors (mock)

---

## 13. QA Checklist

- Keyboard: Tab through all controls, activate via Enter/Space
- Screen Reader: Labels, roles, and `aria-describedby` are correct
- Motion: All animations disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Mobile: Layout stacks gracefully; tabs scroll horizontally
- Theming: Dark mode styles readable and consistent
- Performance: Only `transform` and `opacity` animated; no layout shift

---

## 14. Deliverables

- `/courier/profile` page and all required UI components
- Fully navigable UI demo (no backend)
- README update with instructions for running the frontend demo

---

## 15. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule file and referenced standards
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by project lead

---

**Goal:**
Deliver a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern Courier Account Profile UI, ready for future backend/API integration.

